From: Cyder Engine <cyder@local>
Subject: winemac: Explicitly restore miniaturized windows for Accessibility.

Win32 iconic geometry can clear the Cocoa Miniaturizable style after the
minimize request.  On macOS 27 the inherited AXMinimized=false setter then
returns success without calling deminiaturize: or notifying Win32.
Use the existing native deminiaturize/notification path only for a real
AX restore of a miniaturized window.  Delegate minimize and no-op requests
to AppKit, preserving its validation.  No renderer or game-specific policy.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -2763,6 +2763,17 @@
         [self sendEditMenuCommand:EDIT_COMMAND_UNDO];
     }
 
+    - (void) setAccessibilityMinimized:(BOOL)minimized
+    {
+        /* Explicit AX unminimize uses Cocoa's restore path.  Win32 can remove
+         * the miniaturizable style while iconic, making AppKit's inherited
+         * accessibility setter silently ignore an otherwise valid restore. */
+        if (!minimized && [self isMiniaturized])
+            [self deminiaturize:nil];
+        else
+            [super setAccessibilityMinimized:minimized];
+    }
+
